Subject: [PATCH 211/220] [ae-patch] Park an MCP server's own question as a
 pending elicitation

Claude Code runs an Elicitation hook when an MCP server asks the user something (powerbi-modeling-sp with --require-confirmation, for one). The wrapper never registered it, so the question reached only the TUI. build_hook_settings now registers it beside PermissionRequest with the same day-long timeout, a mcp-elicitation hook subcommand forwards it, and a new route parks it as a permission-type card carrying the server's schema as a form, then returns Claude's hookSpecificOutput. Every failure exits 0 with no output so Claude shows its own dialog.
